    "aliases": ["FORTRESS", "FORTRESS Adversarial", "FORTRESS Benign"],
    "description": "Scale AI national-security and public-safety (NSPS) safeguard eval. The public set has 500 expert adversarial prompts, each with a benign pair and an instance-specific rubric of 4–7 binary questions, across CBRNE, political violence and terrorism, and criminal or financial illicit activity. A panel of LLM judges scores adversarial responses into an average risk score (ARS, 0–100); benign prompts yield an over-refusal score (ORS, 0–100). Lower is better for both.",
    "summary": "Tests whether the model resists adversarial prompts about weapons and violence, while still answering similar safe requests.",
    "maintainers": [
      {
        "name": "Scale AI",
        "url": "https://labs.scale.com/papers/fortress"
      }
    ],
